USA in 60 Seconds · History in 60 Seconds series · Silkscreen Travel Poster style

Picture: drawn in code (Canvas 2D). Print engine engine/silk.js from the Lemo-Opuscar library (MIT).
Landmarks (a platform mound with a timber hall, a brick hall with a steeple, a parchment with a quill, a cannon by a rail fence,
an early biplane over dunes, an Art Deco tower, a rocket above its tower, a suspension bridge in fog) are original stylised
silhouettes drawn as simple paths, not traced from photographs. No logos, no flags or emblems, no maps or borders.

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1; licence texts in fonts/):
  Big Shoulders Display — Patric King / Google Fonts
  Outfit — Rodrigo Fuenzalida / Google Fonts

Voice: Kokoro-82M v1.0 (hexgrad, Apache-2.0) via kokoro-onnx, voice bm_george. Checked with faster-whisper (MIT), model base.en.

Music (original score, music/compose.py): banjo and upright bass by physical modelling (core/audio/pluck.py, Lemo-Opuscar, MIT);
fiddle and washboard synthesised in code. No samples.
Sound (mix.py): paper swish, stamps, a rocket's rumble, river, wind, birds, hooves, a quill and a clock, distant guns, surf,
an aircraft engine, city hum and riveting, a crowd, a foghorn: synthesised in code.
Mastering: FFmpeg (LGPL/GPL) via imageio-ffmpeg.

Facts and sources: FACTS.md.
